  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The London Borough of Hounslow as the Local Planning Authority hereby certify that on 29 July 2003, the matter described above is not lawful within the meaning of section 191 and 192 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 for the following reason:\r\n\r\nThe volume of proposed roof extension incorporating a rear dormer window to the dwelling house at a depth of 2.7m, width of 3.2m and a height of 2.15m, when added to the rear extension, would exceed 50 cubic metres.  \r\n\r\nThe development, therefore, fails to qualify as Class B permitted development within Part 1 of Schedule 2 of The Town and Country Planning (General Permitted Development) Order 1995, and requires planning permission.\r\n"
